stdout: {"type":"sessionUpdate","data":{"sessionId":"sess_2dbc185e-349e-4ad4-b190-9af0d1008beb","update":{"sessionUpdate":"tool_call_update","toolCallId":"toolu_bdrk_019mEPTR6BBfb6RLWA2WdEuu","status":"completed","title":"Read File","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"<file name=\"reanimate-prompt.md\" language=\"markdown\" >\n<content>\n# Reanimate `yahoo-finance-ichart`\n\nWrite a FastAPI server that answers as the dead API did. All files named here are in this directory; use only these relative names.\n\n## Inputs (read only)\n\n- `requirements.md`: the generated spec. Criteria cited below as \"Gen x.y\" are its acceptance criteria.\n- `contract.json`: the inferred API contract.\n- `donor/index.json`: the donor index, keyed by symbol. Each entry names its donor file under `donor/` and its `host` and `served_timestamp`.\n- `error-404.html`: the archived 404 body, served as is for every 404.\n\nDonors available now:\n\n- `AAPL`: `donor/AAPL.csv`, 9086 Data_Rows from 1980-12-12 to 2016-12-21, served by `ichart.finance.yahoo.com` at 20161222215700\n- `MSFT`: `donor/MSFT.csv`, 7819 Data_Rows from 1986-03-13 to 2017-03-17, served by `ichart.yahoo.com` at 20170319115659\n- `YHOO`: `donor/YHOO.csv`, 5162 Data_Rows from 1996-04-12 to 2016-10-12, served by `real-chart.finance.yahoo.com` at 20161013060742\n- `^GSPC`: `donor/%5EGSPC.csv`, 16754 Data_Rows from 1950-01-03 to 2016-08-02, served by `ichart.finance.yahoo.com` at 20160803061104\n\n## Output\n\nWrite exactly one file: `server.py` in this directory, exposing the FastAPI app as `app` (served by `uvicorn server:app`). Create, change or delete no other file.\n\nPython 3.12 style: `X | None`, f-strings.\n\n## Tools\n\nNo shell or command tool is available. Do not run, test or install anything. Only read the inputs and write `server.py`.\n\n## Server rules\n\n1. Route `GET /table.csv` whatever the Host header (Gen 1.1, 1.2, 1.3). Accept and ignore `ignore`, `j`, `q`, `x`, `y` and `z` (Gen 2.8, 2.9, 2.10, 2.12, 2.13, 2.14).\n2. Load `donor/index.json`, the donor files it names and `error-404.html` relative to `Path(__file__).parent`, so responses are identical whatever directory the server starts from. Import only `fastapi`, `uvicorn` and the Python standard library. Make no outbound network request and read no file under `evidence/` (Gen 4.1, 6.1, 7.1).\n3. Check `g` first: a non-empty `g` other than `d` (including `w`, `m`, `v`) answers status 404, `Content-Type: text/html`, the `error-404.html` body and an `X-Revenant-Note: interval <g> is not reanimated yet` header; these intervals are deferred (Gen 2.7).\n4. Then, if `s` is absent, empty or has no entry in `donor/index.json`, answer status 404, `Content-Type: text/html` and the `error-404.html` body, with no CSV content. Query values arrive percent-decoded, so `s=^GSPC` and `s=%5EGSPC` select the same donor and give identical responses (Gen 2.11, 7.1).\n5. Resolve the start date from `a`, `b`, `c` and the end date from `d`, `e`, `f`. If any one of the three is absent, empty or not `int()`-able (for example `c={{(-1 month).year}}`), the whole date is missing: use the earliest Row_Date of the donor for the start and the latest Row_Date for the end (Gen 2.1, 2.2, 2.3, 2.4, 2.5, 2.6, 5.1, 5.2).\n6. Otherwise months are 0-indexed (`a=0` is January): `year = c + a // 12`, `month = a % 12 + 1`, so 12 rolls over to January of the next year and other out-of-range integers roll the same way (inferred); never reject an out-of-range integer. Clamp the day to `1..days_in_month` (inferred). A year outside 1..9999 counts as a missing date (inferred). Never raise an unhandled exception (Gen 3.1, 3.2).\n7. Split the donor file bytes on `b\"\\n\"`. Keep the Data_Rows whose Row_Date lies in `[start, end]`, both inclusive, each copied byte for byte with no reformatting of any number (a zero Volume stays `000`), in the donor's order (newest first) (Gen 4.2, 4.4, 4.7).\n8. Answer status 200, `Content-Type: text/csv`, with the body Header_Line `Date,Open,High,Low,Close,Volume,Adj Close` + `\\n` + each kept row + `\\n` (Gen 4.1, 4.2, 4.4).\n9. If no Data_Row lies in the range (a start after the end included), answer status 404, `Content-Type: text/html` and the `error-404.html` body (Gen 7.1).\n10. Every response, 404 included, carries exactly one `X-Revenant-Donor` header: `wayback:<host>/<served_timestamp>` taken from the `s` entry in `donor/index.json` (its `host` field, not the request's Host header), else `none` (Gen 6.1).\n\n</content>\n</file>"}}],"locations":[{"path":"~\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\revenant-build-c38khpq_\\reanimate-prompt.md"}],"rawInput":{"path":"reanimate-prompt.md","offset":null,"limit":null},"rawOutput":{"message":"<file name=\"reanimate-prompt.md\" language=\"markdown\" >\n<content>\n# Reanimate `yahoo-finance-ichart`\n\nWrite a FastAPI server that answers as the dead API did. All files named here are in this directory; use only these relative names.\n\n## Inputs (read only)\n\n- `requirements.md`: the generated spec. Criteria cited below as \"Gen x.y\" are its acceptance criteria.\n- `contract.json`: the inferred API contract.\n- `donor/index.json`: the donor index, keyed by symbol. Each entry names its donor file under `donor/` and its `host` and `served_timestamp`.\n- `error-404.html`: the archived 404 body, served as is for every 404.\n\nDonors available now:\n\n- `AAPL`: `donor/AAPL.csv`, 9086 Data_Rows from 1980-12-12 to 2016-12-21, served by `ichart.finance.yahoo.com` at 20161222215700\n- `MSFT`: `donor/MSFT.csv`, 7819 Data_Rows from 1986-03-13 to 2017-03-17, served by `ichart.yahoo.com` at 20170319115659\n- `YHOO`: `donor/YHOO.csv`, 5162 Data_Rows from 1996-04-12 to 2016-10-12, served by `real-chart.finance.yahoo.com` at 20161013060742\n- `^GSPC`: `donor/%5EGSPC.csv`, 16754 Data_Rows from 1950-01-03 to 2016-08-02, served by `ichart.finance.yahoo.com` at 20160803061104\n\n## Output\n\nWrite exactly one file: `server.py` in this directory, exposing the FastAPI app as `app` (served by `uvicorn server:app`). Create, change or delete no other file.\n\nPython 3.12 style: `X | None`, f-strings.\n\n## Tools\n\nNo shell or command tool is available. Do not run, test or install anything. Only read the inputs and write `server.py`.\n\n## Server rules\n\n1. Route `GET /table.csv` whatever the Host header (Gen 1.1, 1.2, 1.3). Accept and ignore `ignore`, `j`, `q`, `x`, `y` and `z` (Gen 2.8, 2.9, 2.10, 2.12, 2.13, 2.14).\n2. Load `donor/index.json`, the donor files it names and `error-404.html` relative to `Path(__file__).parent`, so responses are identical whatever directory the server starts from. Import only `fastapi`, `uvicorn` and the Python standard library. Make no outbound network request and read no file under `evidence/` (Gen 4.1, 6.1, 7.1).\n3. Check `g` first: a non-empty `g` other than `d` (including `w`, `m`, `v`) answers status 404, `Content-Type: text/html`, the `error-404.html` body and an `X-Revenant-Note: interval <g> is not reanimated yet` header; these intervals are deferred (Gen 2.7).\n4. Then, if `s` is absent, empty or has no entry in `donor/index.json`, answer status 404, `Content-Type: text/html` and the `error-404.html` body, with no CSV content. Query values arrive percent-decoded, so `s=^GSPC` and `s=%5EGSPC` select the same donor and give identical responses (Gen 2.11, 7.1).\n5. Resolve the start date from `a`, `b`, `c` and the end date from `d`, `e`, `f`. If any one of the three is absent, empty or not `int()`-able (for example `c={{(-1 month).year}}`), the whole date is missing: use the earliest Row_Date of the donor for the start and the latest Row_Date for the end (Gen 2.1, 2.2, 2.3, 2.4, 2.5, 2.6, 5.1, 5.2).\n6. Otherwise months are 0-indexed (`a=0` is January): `year = c + a // 12`, `month = a % 12 + 1`, so 12 rolls over to January of the next year and other out-of-range integers roll the same way (inferred); never reject an out-of-range integer. Clamp the day to `1..days_in_month` (inferred). A year outside 1..9999 counts as a missing date (inferred). Never raise an unhandled exception (Gen 3.1, 3.2).\n7. Split the donor file bytes on `b\"\\n\"`. Keep the Data_Rows whose Row_Date lies in `[start, end]`, both inclusive, each copied byte for byte with no reformatting of any number (a zero Volume stays `000`), in the donor's order (newest first) (Gen 4.2, 4.4, 4.7).\n8. Answer status 200, `Content-Type: text/csv`, with the body Header_Line `Date,Open,High,Low,Close,Volume,Adj Close` + `\\n` + each kept row + `\\n` (Gen 4.1, 4.2, 4.4).\n9. If no Data_Row lies in the range (a start after the end included), answer status 404, `Content-Type: text/html` and the `error-404.html` body (Gen 7.1).\n10. Every response, 404 included, carries exactly one `X-Revenant-Donor` header: `wayback:<host>/<served_timestamp>` taken from the `s` entry in `donor/index.json` (its `host` field, not the request's Host header), else `none` (Gen 6.1).\n\n</content>\n</file>"},"_meta":{"kiro":{"toolOrigin":"default"}}}}}
